    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm managing a rental property in phoenix and the tenant is complaining that the ac is running constantly but one of the bedrooms stays really hot. what are some common reasons why one room would just stay warm like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A common issue in Phoenix! There are several reasons why one room in your rental property might be consistently warm, despite the AC being on. One possibility is that there's a gap or crack in the window or door, allowing warm air to enter or cool air to escape. Another possibility is that the room in question has inadequate insulation or a poor-located AC vent. Additionally, the AC unit itself might be too small or not functioning properly.",
